 Global keys
  1-5                  Sessions; Graph; Quotas; Messages; Tools
  c                    open the Atlas session
  C                    focus the Atlas box for its own keys: enter opens the
                       full Atlas, ctrl+] returns, esc skips a tip
  tab                  move to the next field; back to Sessions
  ?                    help
  /                    filter; find a node; enter selects the first match and
                       esc cancels
  esc                  back; clear or back; Graph; clear
  R                    refresh; rescan
  q, ctrl+c            quit
  enter                go into the selected session in herdr (ctrl+] returns on
                       fallback), or run the selected row's action; detail; open
                       the selected message body; open the selected agent card;
                       select the first match; open Sessions filtered to this
                       agent's project; open the difference plan; open the item
                       details and actions
  up/down, j/k         move the selection; select a conversation; select a
                       subscription; move the selection between nodes; move
  left/right           select the previous message in the conversation; select
                       the next message in the conversation; agent; move the
                       selection between nodes; column

 Sessions
  pgup                 page
  pgdown               page
  home, g              first row
  end                  last row
  m                    send a message to the session as yourself
  n                    start a session in herdr: project, harness, model, folder
                       and first message (a form)
  x                    stop the selected worker or session
  h                    hide or unhide the selected session
  S                    session settings: request rule, delegation policy,
                       integrations, machine name
  v                    cycle the view: active only, all, all with offline, all
                       with offline and hidden
  d                    show or hide the selected session details
  i                    open the inbox
 held request
  a                    approve
  r                    refuse
 learned suggestion
  a                    accept
  r                    reject
 outcome
  s                    let stand
  O                    overrule
 Atlas proposal
  a                    approve
  r                    decline
  A                    approve all

 Graph
  +, =                 zoom in
  -                    zoom out
  shift+left           pan
  shift+right          pan
  shift+up             pan
  shift+down           pan
  ,                    previous neighbour
  .                    next neighbour
  n                    new
 Graph find
  backspace, ctrl+h    delete
 agent card
  n                    start a new session in this project (the same form,
                       filled from here)
  t                    tools
  a                    autonomy
  D                    name project
  u                    undo the selected one (a learned change)
  ,                    previous change
  .                    next change
  h                    hide
  H                    show hidden
  ctrl+d, pgdown       scroll the card: charter, rules and learned changes
  ctrl+u, pgup         scroll the card: charter, rules and learned changes

Legend ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Edges
  ──▶ depends  consumer uses provider
  ──▶ governs  architect over component; mode advisor, arbiter or owner
  ──▶ deploys  deployer runs the app's deploys
  Request rule on an edge from A to B
  normal  delivered; B judges it
  auto    delivered with a trust note; B can act without asking you, still
          inside B's merge authority and refusals
  ask     held in Needs you
  never   refused
  a specific edge beats the all projects wildcard; an edge never grants deploy
  or merge permission by itself (deploy_rule and merge_authority do)
  Charter fields
  maturity         sets the default rules; the only charter field with an
                   enforced effect
  accepts          your agent reads it every turn; every neighbour reads the
                   first 40 characters
  refuses          same as accepts
  escalate         your agent reads it every turn
  purpose          in a worker's brief
  consumers        in a worker's brief
  needs            in a worker's brief, and in the Tools tab
  notes            in a worker's brief
  feature_requests shown only when another agent looks this node up

 Quotas
  p                    protect
  s                    show unset
  d                    details

